#X text 700 180 cycle_slot: one member of a fixed pool implementing buffer_manager.js's cycleTracker sync barrier (see CONVERSION_NOTES.md "buffer_manager: sync barrier"). \$0-scoped [value] storage gives each pooled instance its own isolated state -- no dynamic dict needed. State model: \$0-cid holds the cycleId this slot is tracking\, or -1 if free (no separate owned flag needed -- real cycleIds from slicer_bridge.js are always >= 0). Inlet 0 = "register <cid> <total>" -- claims this slot if free (\$0-cid==-1)\, otherwise passes the message through outlet 0 unchanged so the NEXT slot in the chain gets a turn (wire slot N's outlet 0 -> slot N+1's inlet 0 in buffer_manager.pd). Inlet 1 = "ready <cid> <stemShort>" -- broadcast to every slot in the pool in parallel; only the slot whose \$0-cid matches acts (stemShort itself isn't needed here -- which stems specifically reported in is buffer_manager_stem.pd's job via its own preparedFor tracking\, this object only needs the count). Outlet 1 fires "<cid> all_ready" once \$0-ready reaches \$0-total\, or "<cid> timeout" if [del 250] fires first (250ms\, matching buffer_manager.js's COMMIT_TIMEOUT_MS) -- whichever happens first stops/ignores the other and frees the slot (\$0-cid back to -1) for reuse., f 480;
